1
00:00:00,510 --> 00:00:01,940
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,440
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:09,780
(Episode 26)

4
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:17,220
What have I done today?

5
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:21,990
Kang Da Mi,
what on earth did you just do?

6
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,530
Renewing Song Min Hee's contract
will be difficult.

7
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:33,510
We consider this issue
the store's responsibility as well.

8
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,240
Min Hee is not solely to blame.

9
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:39,180
As the store manager,
I bear more responsibility.

10
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:42,710
It is true that you are not entirely
free from blame, Manager Kang.

11
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,180
However, that does not mean
we can pretend...

12
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:46,580
Song Min Hee's mistake
never happened.

13
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:50,290
In that case...

14
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,760
take disciplinary action
against me instead.

15
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:58,400
Keep Min Hee's contract,
and hold me accountable for this.

16
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,930
Manager Kang,
have you lost your mind?

17
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:05,900
Min Hee has to cover
her father's hospital bills.

18
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,270
She cannot lose her job
over a single mistake.

19
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:11,040
Manager Kang.

20
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:15,650
I personally feel
terrible for Song Min Hee too.

21
00:01:16,050 --> 00:01:18,120
Still, you cannot let your emotions
dictate this situation.

22
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:20,690
Offering to quit your job
in her place...

23
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:22,720
is not something
you should say so lightly.

24
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:25,020
It is not easy.

25
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:27,960
Even so,

26
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,300
it's only right that I take
responsibility.

27
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:32,760
I will take full responsibility.

28
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:44,480
Mom.

29
00:01:44,910 --> 00:01:47,650
Da Mi, did you not say
you were coming home early today?

30
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:49,250
What do you want for dinner?

31
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:52,720
Anything.

32
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:56,490
What? Since when
do you not care what you eat?

33
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:00,330
I just do not have
much of an appetite.

34
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:01,990
I have to hang up.

35
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:08,930
Do not cry. You cannot let it show
at home again.

36
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:16,240
(Office Wear for Women in Their 30s)

37
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:17,880
The clothes are nice,

38
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:21,080
but there is no clear strategy
on who will buy them...

39
00:02:21,150 --> 00:02:22,380
or how to sell them.

40
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:30,190
(K Department Store)

41
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:31,290
That was fast, right?

42
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:35,760
You really did not have to
go through all this trouble.

43
00:02:36,530 --> 00:02:39,500
I should do everything I can.
It is what the customer wants.

44
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:43,700
She has a great sense for retail...

45
00:02:44,070 --> 00:02:46,600
and reads
the buyers' intentions accurately.

46
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:51,280
Right now, what we need
is someone exactly like Kang Da Mi.

47
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:55,710
(Cha Do Yun)

48
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:01,220
Did she sort things out
with her junior colleague?

49
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:11,460
I am back, Team Leader Cha.

50
00:03:12,330 --> 00:03:14,030
Good work, Assistant Manager Kang.

51
00:03:14,870 --> 00:03:17,340
I thought you would stop by
the store, so I waited...

52
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:18,740
I got worried
when you did not show up.

53
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:22,810
I was delayed reviewing
the proposals first.

54
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:25,110
I was just about to head out.

55
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:27,580
Before that,
I will meet with CEO Jeon...

56
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:28,810
and head straight to the site.

57
00:03:30,450 --> 00:03:31,480
Excuse me, Team Leader Cha,

58
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,820
about what happened this morning,

59
00:03:35,390 --> 00:03:37,290
when that department store
employee came by.

60
00:03:38,290 --> 00:03:39,420
Yes, what about it?

61
00:03:39,690 --> 00:03:42,330
May I ask why she came here?

62
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,730
Didn't you say you filed...

63
00:03:48,630 --> 00:03:50,340
the complaint with the store...

64
00:03:50,470 --> 00:03:51,540
for CEO Jeon,
Assistant Manager Kang?

65
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:55,370
Yes. CEO Jeon is very busy,
after all.

66
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:57,680
I see. Just as I thought.

67
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,050
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

68
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,120
Jin Sook.

69
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:14,430
I have done more than enough
for you.

70
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:17,300
You're my only blood relative,

71
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:20,230
and you raised me
in my parents' place.

72
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:22,670
I have already done
far more than enough.

73
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:26,670
You had better not push me anymore.

74
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:28,570
Do you understand?

75
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,510
Son.

76
00:04:36,510 --> 00:04:39,080
I was about to head home early
to prepare for the memorial rite.

77
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:40,720
What is going on?

78
00:04:41,050 --> 00:04:42,690
Please sit down and talk
with me for a moment.

79
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:45,660
All right.

80
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:56,600
By the way, about this morning.

81
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,470
Regarding Manager Kang.

82
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:02,440
Why did you bring her
all the way here yourself?

83
00:05:03,410 --> 00:05:06,080
She knows the job well,
so she caught my interest.

84
00:05:06,910 --> 00:05:07,910
The job?

85
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:11,380
Right now in Product Planning,
we are planning various concepts...

86
00:05:11,450 --> 00:05:12,550
for new product launches...

87
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:14,720
and promoting them
through pop-up stores...

88
00:05:14,790 --> 00:05:17,190
while observing market trends.

89
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:20,960
It is a pity she is only working
as a department store manager now,

90
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:23,590
but she is actually
perfect for the position.

91
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:29,830
So purely as the head
of Product Planning,

92
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:33,240
you think she is such a pro
that you want to work with her,

93
00:05:33,470 --> 00:05:35,870
and that is why you wanted to help?
Is that it?

94
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:39,580
Yes.

95
00:05:40,210 --> 00:05:43,780
That is why I am asking,
if only considering her sincerity...

96
00:05:43,850 --> 00:05:46,820
in coming all the way here
to help her junior colleague,

97
00:05:47,750 --> 00:05:50,460
I would really appreciate it
if you could contact the store, Mom.

98
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:54,130
I'm sorry,
but that's going to be difficult.

99
00:05:55,590 --> 00:05:56,660
Never again...

100
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:59,460
I hope you never bring that up
again, son.

101
00:06:01,470 --> 00:06:02,470
Please leave.

102
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:06,740
And...

103
00:06:08,010 --> 00:06:09,870
Be more careful from now on.

104
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:13,410
The higher the place
you have to climb,

105
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:16,780
the more you must maintain
boundaries with people.

106
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:19,680
Keep my words in mind.

107
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,330
She knows the job well?

108
00:06:35,470 --> 00:06:37,070
A plausible excuse,

109
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:39,200
but you cannot fool my eyes, boy.

110
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:43,540
Do not let just anyone
into your life.

111
00:06:47,110 --> 00:06:53,450
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

112
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:04,060
Your expression looks
heavier than before.

113
00:07:04,730 --> 00:07:06,230
Is it because of the phone call?

114
00:07:08,730 --> 00:07:11,670
Someone I know suddenly
quit her job.

115
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:14,110
She wouldn't tell me why.

116
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:17,440
For some reason,
I cannot stop worrying about her.

117
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,850
Worrying is not a bad thing.

118
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:25,050
However, demanding answers
right away...

119
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:27,590
might make her want
to hide even more.

120
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:30,560
Then what should I do?

121
00:07:32,090 --> 00:07:34,490
Be someone who knows how to wait.

122
00:07:35,030 --> 00:07:38,500
And be someone who is reachable
whenever she needs you.

123
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:41,470
In relationships, maintaining
that kind of distance...

124
00:07:42,070 --> 00:07:44,240
can often be more than enough.

125
00:07:49,570 --> 00:07:50,580
Seung Yun.

126
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,340
Yes?

127
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:55,350
About that day,
the day of the accident long ago.

128
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:58,080
Madam Chairwoman told me...

129
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:00,520
that you have never
mentioned anything...

130
00:08:00,820 --> 00:08:03,150
about what happened that day.

131
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,220
Do you really...

132
00:08:05,890 --> 00:08:08,030
have no memories left at all?

133
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:13,870
Do you want my real answer?

134
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:19,440
Then, Dr. Ju,
you will have to tell me...

135
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,540
the real reason
you are asking me that someday.

136
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,310
You will have to tell me first.

137
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:26,880
Then I will think about it.

138
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,920
How does Dr. Ju manage...

139
00:08:36,250 --> 00:08:39,290
to hang out only with people
who are so good-looking?

140
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:41,930
That black suit is so stylish.

141
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:44,860
Mi Mi!

142
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:48,600
You put in salt twice.
What are you thinking so hard about?

143
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
What? Oh, right.

144
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:54,940
Da Mi is acting strange.

145
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:56,740
What about her?

146
00:08:58,310 --> 00:09:00,910
Whenever I ask her
what she wants for dinner,

147
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:05,520
she always picks something specific.
Soybean paste stew or bulgogi.

148
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:08,290
But today, she said "anything."

149
00:09:08,850 --> 00:09:10,350
She is probably just tired.

150
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:14,090
She acts like that
when something is bothering her.

151
00:09:14,890 --> 00:09:16,390
She pretends she is fine...

152
00:09:16,590 --> 00:09:17,800
and then breaks down
at the dinner table.

153
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:21,700
That girl is tough as nails.
What could happen to her?

154
00:09:21,870 --> 00:09:23,670
She probably just dealt
with a difficult customer.

155
00:09:25,570 --> 00:09:27,200
I have a bad feeling about this.

156
00:09:28,410 --> 00:09:30,170
By the way...

157
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:33,240
Where did Mother go again?

158
00:09:33,910 --> 00:09:35,910
Good question.

159
00:09:36,850 --> 00:09:39,520
You know, Mrs. Choi
has been acting strange lately.

160
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:41,520
She disappears often,

161
00:09:41,990 --> 00:09:44,520
and all she does while working
is grumble and snap at me.

162
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:48,360
She does that to me too.
What is wrong with her?

163
00:09:52,660 --> 00:09:53,760
Hello, this is Kang Dae Chi.

164
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:56,300
Hello, this is the legal team
at B and H.

165
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:59,140
I am calling regarding
the embezzlement allegations.

166
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,310
Yes, please go ahead.

167
00:10:03,170 --> 00:10:06,980
We need a written statement.
We will email you the details.

168
00:10:07,210 --> 00:10:08,480
Please review them...

169
00:10:08,550 --> 00:10:10,150
and submit your statement
and relevant materials...

170
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:11,650
by five o'clock
this Friday afternoon.

171
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:16,790
Does this mean they confirmed...

172
00:10:16,990 --> 00:10:20,060
that I embezzled money?
That is not true, really.

173
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:21,830
It is not confirmed.

174
00:10:22,130 --> 00:10:24,260
We are currently in the process
of verifying the facts.

175
00:10:25,130 --> 00:10:27,630
What if I do not submit it?

176
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:30,900
Whether you submit them or not
is up to you.

177
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:33,200
However, if no explanation
is provided within the deadline,

178
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:35,340
the proceedings may move forward...

179
00:10:35,470 --> 00:10:36,910
based on the materials
gathered so far.

180
00:10:38,710 --> 00:10:42,350
Yes, I understand.
Then you will email me...

181
00:10:42,950 --> 00:10:45,450
You will send the instructions
on how to submit it, right?

182
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:48,890
Yes, yes, thank you.

183
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:57,630
Seriously...

184
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:00,900
Seriously...

185
00:11:23,690 --> 00:11:26,560
You need guts to be a spy.

186
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:30,490
With my old, weary guts,
I really cannot do this.

187
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:42,970
Why does she walk around
with those dark things on her eyes?

188
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:45,540
Does she think she is a movie star
or something?

189
00:11:46,410 --> 00:11:47,810
She clearly has hands...

190
00:11:48,010 --> 00:11:49,810
that have never made fermented paste
in her life.

191
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:53,350
No one should be home at this hour,

192
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:56,220
so I should quietly scoop up
some soybean paste...

193
00:11:56,350 --> 00:11:57,790
and chili paste for them.

194
00:12:03,530 --> 00:12:05,360
What? Grandma.

195
00:12:05,630 --> 00:12:07,630
You scared the living daylights
out of me.

196
00:12:08,330 --> 00:12:11,540
Dae Chi,
why on earth are you sitting there?

197
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:13,500
Why are you so surprised...

198
00:12:13,570 --> 00:12:15,140
to see me in my own house?

199
00:12:15,210 --> 00:12:17,710
It is not your house,
it is your mom's house.

200
00:12:18,210 --> 00:12:19,740
Besides, you always worked late
and came home late,

201
00:12:19,810 --> 00:12:20,810
so I never expected...

202
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:23,850
to see you sitting here
at this hour.

203
00:12:23,950 --> 00:12:26,420
I am working from home
starting this afternoon.

204
00:12:28,490 --> 00:12:31,090
If you are working from home,
you should be working.

205
00:12:31,490 --> 00:12:32,620
You're young, yet you sit around...

206
00:12:32,690 --> 00:12:35,790
eating snacks meant for children
and wasting time.

207
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:40,460
If your company catches you,
you will be fired on the spot.

208
00:12:41,570 --> 00:12:42,830
Grandma,

209
00:12:43,730 --> 00:12:45,600
why do you have to say
such terrible things?

210
00:12:48,110 --> 00:12:51,010
Take it away or clean it up!
Who do you expect to do it?

211
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:56,580
Wait a minute, Dae Chi.

212
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:00,580
Are you really the only one home?

213
00:13:01,190 --> 00:13:03,420
No, Da Mi came home early too.

214
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:06,260
What do you mean?

215
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:10,060
- Did she say she was sick?
- She seemed fine.

216
00:13:10,690 --> 00:13:13,130
She is in her room.
She told me not to bother her.

217
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:17,100
All right, got it.
Go on upstairs, hurry.

218
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:19,600
Okay.

219
00:13:34,150 --> 00:13:37,190
Why is she picking on me?
I have enough on my mind.

220
00:13:41,590 --> 00:13:42,590
(Hwanggeum Brat)

221
00:13:43,830 --> 00:13:45,960
Am I her only account?

222
00:13:46,460 --> 00:13:47,460
She is so persistent.

223
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:57,580
He promised to send a repayment plan
for the principal,

224
00:13:58,010 --> 00:13:59,880
and now he is ignoring
all my calls again.

225
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:02,910
Then I will call his office.

226
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,890
Hello, may I speak
to Manager Kang Dae Chi...

227
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:16,360
in the purchasing department?

228
00:14:18,830 --> 00:14:19,830
Pardon?

229
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:22,270
He is away from his desk again?

230
00:14:23,430 --> 00:14:25,740
This is my sixth call. How can he...

231
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:26,870
keep being away from his desk?

232
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:29,570
I cannot reach his cell phone,

233
00:14:30,110 --> 00:14:31,140
and I am really worried.

234
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:34,850
Pardon?

235
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,820
Suspended from duty?

236
00:14:47,060 --> 00:14:50,160
She certainly brought over
a wide variety of side dishes.

237
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:51,730
Why are you eating alone, though?

238
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:53,760
If you want some,

239
00:14:53,830 --> 00:14:55,170
dish yourself a bowl of rice
and join me.

240
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:58,800
No, I am not in the mood.

241
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:03,910
Anyway, Ye Ri's dad.

242
00:15:05,510 --> 00:15:07,750
- What?
- Your mother...

243
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:09,980
Do not let her come
to this house anymore.

244
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:13,650
- Why?
- Do you really need to ask?

245
00:15:14,790 --> 00:15:16,750
A mother and son
reuniting after decades...

246
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:19,260
is heart-wrenching and emotional,
and I understand that.

247
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,860
However, you have to think
about Ye Ri.

248
00:15:21,190 --> 00:15:23,960
If Ye Ri finds out about this,
what will you tell her?

249
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:26,000
How will you explain
the existence...

250
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:28,070
of a grandma who suddenly
appeared out of nowhere?

251
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:32,340
No secret lasts forever
in this world.

252
00:15:33,470 --> 00:15:34,510
What?

253
00:15:35,070 --> 00:15:38,540
Are you saying right now
that you are willing to lay bare...

254
00:15:38,580 --> 00:15:42,150
our entire family history to Ye Ri?
Are you truly okay with that?

255
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:45,450
Even a shameful history
is still history.

256
00:15:45,950 --> 00:15:47,250
Brace yourself.

257
00:15:48,750 --> 00:15:50,850
We cannot keep it hidden forever.

258
00:15:53,190 --> 00:15:55,290
Are you out of your mind?
Absolutely not.

259
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:04,970
What did you want to say?

260
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:08,570
You know Hyung Gu, right?

261
00:16:08,770 --> 00:16:11,810
- He sent over a box of apples.
- An apple box?

262
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:13,340
Why?

263
00:16:14,850 --> 00:16:16,210
What about the loan
you co-signed for him?

264
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,380
Did he pay it back?

265
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:21,250
Well, not that. Just listen to me.

266
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:23,050
Why are you so impatient?

267
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:26,690
Anyway...

268
00:16:27,830 --> 00:16:30,360
You know his wife
is Vietnamese, right?

269
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,230
You met her once before.

270
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:38,640
She went back to Vietnam
and started a travel agency,

271
00:16:39,670 --> 00:16:42,940
and it is doing quite well.
So he is leaving Korea...

272
00:16:43,010 --> 00:16:44,480
to go help her out.

273
00:16:45,510 --> 00:16:49,780
Then what about our money?
Before he packs up or gets lost,

274
00:16:49,850 --> 00:16:52,380
should he not pay back the money
we covered by co-signing for him?

275
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:55,290
Calling me out here
just to talk nonsense.

276
00:16:56,590 --> 00:16:58,790
I am the fool
for momentarily forgetting...

277
00:16:58,860 --> 00:17:01,290
that you cannot be reasoned with.

278
00:17:02,490 --> 00:17:06,900
Hey, please.
Just hear me out, will you?

279
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,730
So, I asked him.

280
00:17:10,470 --> 00:17:12,540
I asked what he would do
with the factory.

281
00:17:12,870 --> 00:17:15,710
Then he asked me...

282
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:18,080
if I was interested
in taking it over...

283
00:17:18,140 --> 00:17:19,140
for 50,000 dollars.

284
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:21,910
What?

285
00:17:21,910 --> 00:17:24,010
Think of how well I have treated him
all this time.

286
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:27,150
Besides, look,
in this great age of AI,

287
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:30,650
handing over a factory like that
for 50,000 dollars...

288
00:17:30,850 --> 00:17:32,390
is an incredible deal.

289
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:34,390
I really think this...

290
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:38,560
is the final opportunity
heaven is giving me.

291
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:41,700
Listen here, Kang Gang Nam.

292
00:17:42,230 --> 00:17:43,700
Why do you not finish
that story first?

293
00:17:44,570 --> 00:17:46,900
That box of apples
your friend Lee Hyung Gu sent over.

294
00:17:47,140 --> 00:17:48,770
Those were not real apples,
were they?

295
00:17:49,570 --> 00:17:51,640
What was inside?

296
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:54,980
What do you mean, what was inside?
Things made at his factory.

297
00:17:55,810 --> 00:17:57,050
Phone stands.

298
00:17:58,020 --> 00:18:02,790
He sent about 300 of them.
They are so well made...

299
00:18:02,850 --> 00:18:04,760
- that the phone will not slip out.
- Hey, Kang Gang Nam.

300
00:18:05,060 --> 00:18:06,660
Are you an idiot? A total sucker?

301
00:18:08,030 --> 00:18:11,230
What do phone stands have to do
with the great AI era?

302
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:13,930
If you prop up a phone using AI,
does that make it an AI business?

303
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,500
Then what about an internet cafe
filled with computers?

304
00:18:16,670 --> 00:18:18,300
Is that a quantum
computing industry?

305
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:20,840
Hey.

306
00:18:21,410 --> 00:18:22,910
Why do you have to talk like that?

307
00:18:23,270 --> 00:18:25,540
You still have a long way to go
before you come to your senses.

308
00:18:26,410 --> 00:18:28,810
How much more do you have to lose
to snap out of it?

309
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:31,580
Wait, no.

310
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:34,450
Do you even have anything
left to lose?

311
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:40,560
Hey, Kim Mi Seon.
Are you quite finished?

312
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:44,530
Looking down on me
until the very end.

313
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,870
She really acts like
she is all that.

314
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:49,200
So full of herself.

315
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:55,670
Seriously,
throwing a tantrum like that...

316
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:57,340
(K Department Store VIP Luxury Hall
Kang Da Mi)

317
00:18:57,410 --> 00:18:58,780
(Manager Kang Da Mi)

318
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:01,450
Manager Kang Da Mi.

319
00:19:03,050 --> 00:19:04,580
It is really over now.

320
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:16,330
Hello? Who is this?

321
00:19:17,330 --> 00:19:18,330
Kang Da Mi,

322
00:19:18,430 --> 00:19:20,560
this is Team Leader Cha Do Yun
from Hwanggeum Apparel.

323
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:25,400
Hello, Team Leader Cha.
What can I do for you?

324
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:28,370
Well, I was hoping
to meet with you briefly, Da Mi.

325
00:19:28,570 --> 00:19:30,110
Do you have time right now?

326
00:19:31,070 --> 00:19:32,280
Right now?

327
00:19:39,050 --> 00:19:40,780
I must have startled you
by asking to meet out of the blue.

328
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:43,520
Thank you for coming, Da Mi.

329
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:45,620
You came all the way
to my neighborhood,

330
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:46,990
so I should be the one thanking you.

331
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:51,700
What was it you wanted to discuss,
Team Leader Cha?

332
00:19:54,030 --> 00:19:55,970
I called the boutique to check.

333
00:19:56,670 --> 00:19:58,770
I heard you quit
the department store.

334
00:20:00,470 --> 00:20:01,910
Yes, that is what happened.

335
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:04,740
Did you resign...

336
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:08,710
because of our CEO's complaint...

337
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:11,580
Please tell me what is on your mind.

338
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:14,650
All right, then.

339
00:20:21,590 --> 00:20:23,030
Please take a look at this.

340
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:24,660
What is this?

341
00:20:25,130 --> 00:20:27,970
A proposal for Hwanggeum Apparel's
pop-up store project.

342
00:20:28,130 --> 00:20:30,570
We need someone who knows
the ins and outs of boutique retail.

343
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:32,000
As the team leader in charge,

344
00:20:32,070 --> 00:20:34,870
I am making you an offer
to scout you, Da Mi.

345
00:20:36,010 --> 00:20:39,480
Of course, from your perspective,
it will not be a bad offer.

346
00:20:43,110 --> 00:20:46,580
I truly believe
you would do an amazing job.

347
00:20:51,050 --> 00:20:52,990
This is so sudden...

348
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:56,590
Let me think about it first.

349
00:20:57,890 --> 00:21:00,830
Sure, take a few days to think
and then let me know.

350
00:21:06,070 --> 00:21:08,740
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

351
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:24,320
I think everything
is ready now, CEO Jeon.

352
00:21:24,790 --> 00:21:25,920
Wait a moment.

353
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:29,230
- Please move it a bit further in.
- Yes, ma'am.

354
00:21:33,630 --> 00:21:34,670
It takes so much work...

355
00:21:35,170 --> 00:21:36,670
every time, does it not?

356
00:21:37,070 --> 00:21:38,740
It is what I have
always done, Mother.

357
00:21:40,570 --> 00:21:41,910
You work so hard.

358
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,570
It is only natural.

359
00:21:59,390 --> 00:22:01,560
Yes. Go ahead and offer it.

360
00:22:27,750 --> 00:22:28,890
Father, Mother.

361
00:22:29,450 --> 00:22:31,190
I am offering the cup
myself this year.

362
00:22:32,190 --> 00:22:34,560
I want to tell you
that I am doing well,

363
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:37,160
but I am not so sure yet.

364
00:23:05,690 --> 00:23:07,220
Still, I am hanging in there.

365
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:08,960
So,

366
00:23:09,930 --> 00:23:11,460
please watch over me
a little longer.

367
00:23:17,930 --> 00:23:19,540
Now, let us partake
in the memorial food.

368
00:23:24,010 --> 00:23:26,480
- Take a sip of the drink.
- Yes, Uncle.

369
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:34,790
All right.

370
00:23:34,850 --> 00:23:37,750
Now we share the food,
and then we can clear the table.

371
00:23:38,050 --> 00:23:39,060
Yes.

372
00:23:42,690 --> 00:23:43,690
Yes, Father.

373
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:07,880
Father...

374
00:24:08,350 --> 00:24:09,350
Mother.

375
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:12,020
The accident we had to go through
that day...

376
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:14,590
was not just an accident, was it?

377
00:24:15,730 --> 00:24:17,330
Someone did that to you...

378
00:24:18,660 --> 00:24:21,000
I will get to the bottom of this,
no matter what.

379
00:24:21,570 --> 00:24:23,670
Because that must be
the reason I survived.

380
00:24:37,580 --> 00:24:39,350
- All right.
- Yes, Grandma.

381
00:24:42,690 --> 00:24:43,690
Yes.

382
00:24:45,190 --> 00:24:47,790
Even when Jun Sung was your age,

383
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:50,760
he rarely shared
what was on his mind.

384
00:24:52,430 --> 00:24:53,930
Do I take after my father?

385
00:24:55,030 --> 00:24:56,030
You do.

386
00:24:56,530 --> 00:24:58,970
Right down to keeping
all your hardships...

387
00:24:59,070 --> 00:25:00,200
bottled up inside.

388
00:25:02,410 --> 00:25:06,980
However, there is a limit
to enduring things alone.

389
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:10,450
When you are beside someone
who keeps quiet,

390
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:12,050
waiting for them to speak first...

391
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:16,020
waiting until they open up
is necessary, of course,

392
00:25:16,650 --> 00:25:20,190
but you must not let it be too late.

393
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:24,360
At my age,
I have come to realize that.

394
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:31,500
If someone comes along
whom you cannot lose,

395
00:25:32,370 --> 00:25:35,710
you must reach out to them first
before it is too late.

396
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:40,040
Keep in mind that is the only way...

397
00:25:40,140 --> 00:25:42,450
you will avoid a lifetime of regret.

398
00:25:44,010 --> 00:25:45,050
Yes, Grandma.

399
00:25:45,850 --> 00:25:48,550
Good. Stay, stay. It is all right.

400
00:25:50,590 --> 00:25:52,220
- Get down safely, Grandma.
- All right.

401
00:26:10,210 --> 00:26:12,380
(Manager Kang Da Mi)

402
00:26:28,260 --> 00:26:29,330
That scared me.

403
00:26:30,530 --> 00:26:31,860
Who is it
in the middle of the night?

404
00:26:34,530 --> 00:26:36,900
What does he want now?

405
00:26:42,470 --> 00:26:43,510
Hello?

406
00:26:43,940 --> 00:26:44,940
I see you were awake.

407
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:46,740
I am so sorry to call this late.

408
00:26:48,080 --> 00:26:49,180
What is going on?

409
00:26:50,410 --> 00:26:53,080
There is something
I really need to give you.

410
00:26:54,150 --> 00:26:55,920
To me? What...

411
00:26:57,290 --> 00:26:58,360
You'll know when you see it.

412
00:26:58,890 --> 00:27:00,960
I would like to meet now
and give it to you in person.

413
00:27:01,930 --> 00:27:02,960
Right now?

414
00:27:04,290 --> 00:27:05,660
Yes, if you can, that is.

415
00:27:07,700 --> 00:27:11,770
I am at a shop
near my house right now.

416
00:27:12,970 --> 00:27:14,670
Then could you send me the address?

417
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:17,670
You do not have to come
all the way here...

418
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:20,280
I really need to hand it to you
in person.

419
00:27:55,750 --> 00:27:57,710
(Mission: Mompossible)

420
00:28:18,540 --> 00:28:20,700
When did you write all of this down?

421
00:28:21,470 --> 00:28:23,940
I quit my job
at the department store.

422
00:28:24,340 --> 00:28:26,340
Why on earth would Team Leader Cha
be so happy...

423
00:28:26,410 --> 00:28:27,740
to get her call
and rush out like that?

424
00:28:27,940 --> 00:28:30,150
Mother, the side dishes
and kimchi in the fridge...

425
00:28:30,210 --> 00:28:32,150
Did you happen to give them
to someone?

426
00:28:32,550 --> 00:28:34,550
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
